@startuml usecase
' Use case diagram for the COLORS web application (COP 4331 LAMP lab).
' Based on public/js/code.js and the PHP files in api/.
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "User" as User
actor "MySQL Database\n(COP4331)" as DB <<system>>

rectangle "COLORS Web Application" {
  usecase "Log In" as UC_Login
  usecase "Search Colors" as UC_Search
  usecase "Add Color" as UC_Add
  usecase "Log Out" as UC_Logout
}

' Primary actor
User -- UC_Login
User -- UC_Search
User -- UC_Add
User -- UC_Logout

' Secondary actor: only the use cases that call a PHP endpoint touch MySQL
UC_Login -- DB
UC_Search -- DB
UC_Add -- DB

legend bottom
  | Use case | Implementation |
  | Log In | index.html, doLogin() -> POST /LAMPAPI/Login.php. Matches Login and Password in Users. On success a cookie (firstName, lastName, userId) is saved for 20 minutes and color.html opens. |
  | Search Colors | color.html, searchColor() -> POST /LAMPAPI/SearchColors.php. Returns Colors whose Name contains the text, only for the logged-in userId. |
  | Add Color | color.html, addColor() -> POST /LAMPAPI/AddColor.php. Inserts (UserId, Name) into Colors. |
  | Log Out | doLogout() expires the cookie and returns to index.html. No API or database call. |
  Precondition for Search Colors, Add Color and Log Out: the user is logged in. readCookie() runs once when
  color.html loads and sends the user back to index.html if the cookie has no userId.
  Not in this system: registration, editing or deleting colors. Users are added to MySQL directly.
endlegend
@enduml
